  "n12" [label="(12,0,0) Deduction-case: Currently there is the varied nature of exchange interactions allows heterointerfacing different types of magnetism in a superlattice to induce magnetic frustration through proximity coupling."];
  "n13" [label="(13,0,0) Abduction-knowledge: If we demonstrate a heterostructure-based strategy to frustrate the Néel AF order in square-lattice iridates, then quantum fluctuations can be measured and spinons revealed via specific x-ray techniques."];
  "n14" [label="(14,0,0) Deduction-case: Currently there is time-resolved resonant x-ray diffraction (RXD) is used to measure quantum fluctuations via recovery dynamics of AF order after optical pump, slowing with enhanced frustration."];
  "n15" [label="(15,0,0) Deduction-case: Currently there is polarization-resolved resonant inelastic x-ray scattering (RIXS) and high-energy-resolution RIXS are used to reveal the absence of single magnons in most part of the Brillouin zone away from the immediate vicinity of the ordering wavevector."];
  "n16" [label="(16,0,0) Abduction-knowledge: If the spectra are dominated by isotropic continua instead of single magnons, then this provides compelling evidence for spinons in a square-lattice Heisenberg AF."];
